/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
558 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E (Conventional Business Intelligence tools are generally designed for structured numerical data and often struggle to process unstructured textual information effectively. Without advanced Natural Language Processing techniques, extracting meaningful sentiment information from raw customer reviews remains difficult.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
559 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E (In addition, simple keyword-based approaches frequently fail to capture contextual meaning within customer opinions. Words may express different sentiments depending on context, especially in the presence of negation, sarcasm, or mixed emotional expressions.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
560 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E (Many traditional systems also face scalability limitations when handling Big Data environments. Processing large volumes of customer reviews requires efficient storage, distributed processing capabilities, and optimized analytical workflows.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
561 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E (Furthermore, certain existing sentiment analysis approaches rely heavily on manually defined rules, which reduces flexibility and limits their ability to generalize across different datasets and review contexts.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
562 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
